// error: `map` is already a method of `Mappable[A]` with the same parameter types, which a call always finds first; an extension adds methods the type does not have
// error: `twice` is ambiguous on Option[Option[int]]: module `left` and module `right` each add it with the same parameter types, and this file sees both
// error: `label` is ambiguous on Option[int]: module `left` and module `right` each add it with the same parameter types, and this file sees both
// Two extensions a file sees, from different modules, that add a method of one name and parameter
// types to the applications of constructor parameters a receiver matches make a call of it an
// error naming both modules; a call on a receiver only one of them matches is not. An extension
// cannot add the bound's own method.
import left
import right

main()
  println(Some(Some(1)).twice((o: Option[int]) -> o))
  println(Some(1).label())
  println(Some(1).twice((n: int) -> n + 1))
